# Afenda ERP app (`apps/erp`)

Full agent context: `AGENTS.md` (repo root). System runtime: **ARCH-1001**.

## Next.js DevTools MCP

When working on `apps/erp` (routes, RSC, handlers, caching, or Next.js APIs), call the **`init` tool** from the **next-devtools** MCP server at the **start of the session** (or when the task clearly shifts to Next.js app work). That loads version-matched Next.js guidance before you write or change code.

- Project MCP: `.cursor/mcp.json` → `next-devtools` (`npx -y next-devtools-mcp@latest`).
- Still read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` for breaking changes (see root `AGENTS.md`).
- Repo doctrine (**ARCH-1001**, tenancy, governed UI) overrides generic Next.js defaults from MCP.

## Route ownership

- Authenticated shell: route group `(workspace)/` (Next.js route groups — omitted from URL). `layout.tsx` renders `ShellFrame` immediately; sidebar/header load in parallel `<Suspense>` boundaries (`workspace-routes/*.server.tsx`).
- Dynamic module workspace: `(workspace)/[moduleId]/` — thin `page.tsx` only; compose governed surfaces from `@/workspace-routes/*`. Do not add `finance/`, `sales/`, etc. as sibling route folders unless the URL tree is genuinely different.
- Do not put non-route TSX under `src/app/` — use `src/workspace-routes/` (matches Next.js “store project files outside of app”).
- Dashboard and Lynx (`/lynx`) are dedicated routes, not `[moduleId]`.
- `src/proxy.ts` is the Next.js 16 traffic/session helper — not the sole auth boundary.

## Server vs client

- Default to Server Components; Client Components only for grids, palettes, uploads, charts, optimistic forms.
- Lazy-init DB/auth via package helpers (`getDb()`, `@afenda/auth/server`). No module-scope pools or SDK clients in new code.
- Batch independent RSC reads with `Promise.all` where safe.

## HTTP API (**ARCH-1004** — target only)

- **Required tree:** `src/app/api/internal/v1/…` (Lynx, AI, cron, webhooks) and `public/v1/…` (partners). `src/app/api/auth/` is the Neon Auth exception.
- **Wrong:** flat `src/app/api/lynx/`, `api/ai/`, `api/cron/` — hook **denies** writes (rule `afenda-agent-discipline`).
- **`route.ts`:** ≤15 lines — auth, Zod parse, dispatch to `@afenda/feature-*/server` or `@afenda/api`. **No** `@afenda/db`, `streamText`, or domain logic in routes.
- **`src/lib/api/`:** no module Zod, Lynx, or HR business logic — only shared non-module helpers (e.g. chat/solution-provider request schemas). Feature schemas live in `packages/features/*/schemas/`.
- Lynx paths: **ARCH-1004** §5 and `packages/features/lynx/AGENTS.md`.

## Handlers and mutations

- **Server Actions** — dispatch same `commands/` as HTTP; permissions before domain; narrow revalidation after writes.
- **Route Handlers** — thin transport only (see above).
- **Cron** — `POST /api/internal/v1/cron/<job>` + `CRON_SECRET` (`src/lib/cron.ts`). Flat `api/cron/*` is non-compliant.

## Caching (Next 16 Cache Components)

- Tenant-scoped lists and dashboards: dynamic reads inside org context — do not CDN-cache another tenant's rows.
- `'use cache'` / `'use cache: remote'` only for shared reference data; prefer `cache: 'no-store'` over blanket `force-dynamic` when one subtree must stay fresh.

## Feature package imports

- Import `@afenda/feature-*` through public doors only (`.`, `./client`, `./server`, `./metadata`) — never `/src`, `/dist`, or `/internal`.
- Routes and Server Components: prefer `./server` or `./metadata`; Client Components: `./client` only.
- Adding a workspace dependency requires the same package in `afendaTranspilePackages` (`packages/config/src/next.ts`). **ARCH-1005**.

## Governed lists in this app

- Compose `GovernedPatternCListSection` from `@afenda/governed-surface/server`.
- Builders today: `@afenda/kernel` (`src/modules/list-surfaces.ts`); move to `@afenda/feature-*` when extracting.
- Pass validated **configuration** to client bridges, not raw Drizzle rows.
